 x^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 24 x.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577247 1072 #uuid "53a41d24-47c9-59a3-bb8f-2ba3ae6870d8" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577247 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 6 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 6 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-6\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 12 x \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - 24 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 6 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 12 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3 y}{x} \\\\ - 12 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3\\left(- 6 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 12 x &\\not\\equiv - 18 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 6 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577248 1080 "false" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577248 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577248 1083 #uuid "5748cdfc-a23f-59d4-91c2-ae08e9280e33" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577249 1080 "false" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577249 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577249 1083 #uuid "57dd76c7-1580-54a7-8702-832f92b56a36" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577250 1075 #edb/ref 1759