rset{?}{=}\\frac{3 y}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\not\\equiv - 15 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 5 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577252 1080 "false" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577252 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577252 1083 #uuid "646a3baf-7c68-5935-a198-a09a52711555" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577253 1080 "true" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577253 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577253 1083 #uuid "6c95be75-7cdb-5526-881d-fedce4e80ff4" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577254 1080 "true" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577254 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577254 1083 #uuid "702a4e6a-ff6b-521c-a157-521109dc3428" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577241 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577255 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577272 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577255 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577255 1077 "I" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577255 1078 #edb/ref 17592186577272 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577255 1079 #uuid "71481ca8-e7c8-5dea-9ec6-cf7e74d010d1" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577256 1068 #edb/ref 17592186577242 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577256 1068 #edb/ref 17592186577250 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577256 1068 #edb/ref 17592186577277 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577256 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577256 1071 "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{4 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 2 x^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 8 x^{3}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577256 1072 #uuid "729ec480-d7e2-58dc-a850-b9ff69610ca0" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577256 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 x^{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 x^{4}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot 4 x^{3} \\\\ &=- 8 x^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=- 2 x^{4}$ and $y\\prime=- 8 x^{3}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\left(- 2 x^{4}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &=- 8 x^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=- 2 x^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577257 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577246 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577257 1075 #edb/ref 17592186577249 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577257 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577257 1077 "I" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577257 1078 #edb/ref 17592186577249 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577257 1079 #uuid "7a0c4a37-dc9b-5b7b-98ce-2b41b1443ec4" 13194139537007 17592186045443 true] [17592186577258 1080 "false" 1319